comments:
I tested to modify the `loadFile`-function locally to try and resolve files relative to all include paths, not just current directory. This seems to work. Not sure if it is enough to create a PR.

In `.lessrc`
```json
{
    "paths": [
        "../node_modules/foo/bar/"
    ]
}
```

In https://github.com/parcel-bundler/parcel/blob/master/packages/core/parcel-bundler/src/assets/LESSAsset.js#L83-L93
```javascript
async loadFile(filename, currentDirectory) {
  filename = parseCSSImport(filename);

  const directories = [
    currentDirectory,
    ...less.importManager.context.paths.map(
      includePath => path.resolve(options.rootDir, includePath)
    )
  ];
  let resolved, err;
  for (let directory of directories) {
    try {
      resolved = await resolver.resolve(
        filename,
        path.join(directory, 'index')
      );
      break;
    } catch (e) {
      err = e;
    }
  }

  if (!resolved) {
    throw err;
  }

  return {
    contents: await fs.readFile(resolved.path, 'utf8'),
    filename: resolved.path
  };
}
```

Example:
If file at `./src/index.less` contains:
```
@import "baz";
```
It will find the file at `./src/baz.less`, but if that doesn't exist it will also look for `./node_modules/foo/bar/baz.less`

